From: Adam Hillson <598804+BadAd84@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] glm: a solo prompt step runs between request starts

TF_GLM_REQUEST_STARTS=1 cuts a prompt pass at each message start, and a request with any cut took no solo step
(TF_GLM_CHUNK_SOLO=4096): prompt_solo.at, prompt_solo.allowed and cuda_prompt_cuts.stepRows each refused a solo-sized
step when the request had a cut. The server's chunk plan (chunk_plan.Plan.starts) lists a start at every grid step from
the last start as well as at each message, so every chat request under request starts ran in 2,048-row steps. On three
GB10s at TP=3 a cold first token with request starts read 4.1%, 6.5% and 7.2% slower than without at 8k, 32k and 120k,
within 1% of the CHUNK_SOLO-only arm, and a ~113k cold prime 7.3% slower.

The cold plan is unchanged: a pass cuts every 2,048 rows from 0 and at each start (nextCut, coldCut), and a kept
state resumes only at a cold cut (resumes, below). A solo step is two such chunks run as one pass: the plan's next
chunk ends at start + 2,048 and the one after it at the step's end. The cut between them is a start the plan lists at
every grid step, so cutInside leaves the step's middle grid point out: a start is inside a step only after its first
row, before its end and off that point. prompt_solo.at (rank 0's choice), prompt_solo.allowed (every rank's check of the
step) and stepRows (the part's length) all use it, so the ranks agree on every step; takesTwo still refuses a step
whose middle grid point holds a keep mark. A request with no cut is unchanged: cutInside is false for an empty list.
Pairing (TF_GLM_PROMPT_PAIR) still refuses a request with cuts.

The grid from a message start is off the 4-row pool's edge for three starts in four, and the index rings held a solo
pass's rows only from a pool's edge: State.ready floors a rebase to the pool below the pass's first row, so a
4,096-row step from row 4,096 + r (r 1 to 3) ended in error.PastRing. index_ring grows by one pool over the new
solo_rows (2 * prefill_rows, what it was). The plain grid starts every step on a multiple of 2,048, where the rings
rebase exactly as before. A kept state's image and the disk store's identity carry the ring's size, so a store
written before this change is not read.

Replies are CHUNK_SOLO's: upstream's contract is the same tokens as 2,048-row passes. Receipts: host tests of
cuda_prompt_cuts (stepRows and cutInside, and a walk over lists shaped as the server sends them, whose solo steps
are exactly the steps whose next two plan chunks are the grid's two), of cuda_prompt_solo (rank 0's choice and the
check, at a start on and off the pool's edge) and of State.ready at each start residue. The GPU receipts (cold first
token and replies with request starts on and solo on, against solo alone and request starts alone) are not in this
header.

New here, not a re-seat: written at v1.2.9 on top of this repo's stack (patches/engine, pr1411, cache-salt and
learn-starts). Its docs hunk sits on learn-starts' text of the request starts paragraph, which now says that a pass
with starts takes a solo pass where no message start is inside it.

